        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Dr732kjv7UyW1QPMPvEX-41" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" value="Two safety nets, because voiding the link can fail&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Voiding runs AFTER the commit and never throws: it is a network call to PayOS,&lt;br&gt;and holding database locks across a network wait is how deadlocks are made.&lt;br&gt;If it fails, the link stays alive and someone can still pay a cancelled order.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The second net catches that. The payment webhook now checks the order status&lt;br&gt;first: if the order is cancelled the money is credited to the BUYER WALLET and&lt;br&gt;the order stays cancelled — see 06-activity-diagram. It cannot be ignored,&lt;br&gt;because the money is already in the real bank account; not recording it would&lt;br&gt;put gateway_clearing out of step with the bank.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Until 14 Aug neither net existed: the webhook set status = confirmed without&lt;br&gt;looking, so a cancelled order came back to life while its stock had already&lt;br&gt;been returned to the shelf." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="800" x="1440" y="1500" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
